# QR Code Scanner Addon

## When to Use This Addon

Use the QR Scanner addon when you need to:
- Scan product barcodes for inventory management
- Read QR codes for authentication or verification
- Check-in attendees at events
- Track assets with QR labels
- Link physical items to digital records
- Enable quick data entry via QR codes
- Implement contactless information sharing

## Browser Compatibility

**Supported Browsers:**
- Chrome/Chromium (desktop & mobile)
- Edge (desktop & mobile)
- Samsung Internet
- Opera

**Not Supported:**
- Safari/iOS (shows error message)
- Firefox (shows error message)

**Recommendation**: Display a warning or alternative input method for unsupported browsers.

## Basic Implementation

```jsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import QRScanner from '@addons/qr-scanner/QRScanner';

export default function MyComponent({ jcontext }) {
  const [isQROpen, setIsQROpen] = useState(false);
  const [scannedValue, setScannedValue] = useState('');

  const handleScan = async (value) => {
    console.log('Scanned:', value);
    setScannedValue(value);

    // Query database with scanned value
    try {
      const db = jcontext.app.db.use('products');
      const result = await db.fetch({ qr_code: value });

      if (result && result.length > 0) {
        // Product found
        console.log('Product:', result[0]);
      }
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Database error:', error);
    }
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <button onClick={() => setIsQROpen(true)}>
        Scan QR Code
      </button>

      <QRScanner
        isOpen={isQROpen}
        onClose={() => setIsQROpen(false)}
        onScan={handleScan}
      />

      {scannedValue && <p>Last scanned: {scannedValue}</p>}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Common Use Cases

### 1. Product Inventory Scanner

```jsx
const handleProductScan = async (qrCode) => {
  const db = jcontext.app.db.use('inventory');

  // Check if product exists
  const product = await db.fetch({ qr_code: qrCode });

  if (product && product.length > 0) {
    // Update quantity or load product details
    setCurrentProduct(product[0]);
    jcontext.app.ui.toast('Product loaded!', 'success');
  } else {
    jcontext.app.ui.toast('Product not found', 'error');
  }
};

<QRScanner
  isOpen={isScannerOpen}
  onClose={() => setIsScannerOpen(false)}
  onScan={handleProductScan}
  title="Scan Product QR"
  successMessage="Product found!"
/>
```

### 2. Event Check-In System

```jsx
const handleCheckIn = async (ticketCode) => {
  const db = jcontext.app.db.use('tickets');

  try {
    const ticket = await db.fetch({ code: ticketCode });

    if (!ticket || ticket.length === 0) {
      jcontext.app.ui.toast('Invalid ticket', 'error');
      return;
    }

    if (ticket[0].checked_in) {
      jcontext.app.ui.toast('Already checked in!', 'warning');
      return;
    }

    // Mark as checked in
    await db.update(ticket[0].id, {
      checked_in: true,
      checked_in_at: new Date().toISOString()
    });

    jcontext.app.ui.toast(`Welcome, ${ticket[0].attendee_name}!`, 'success');
  } catch (error) {
    jcontext.app.ui.toast('Check-in failed', 'error');
  }
};

<QRScanner
  isOpen={isCheckInOpen}
  onClose={() => setIsCheckInOpen(false)}
  onScan={handleCheckIn}
  title="Scan Ticket"
  autoCloseDelay={2000}
/>
```

